            <ArticleTitle>Aneurysm of coronary sinus of Valsalva can rupture anytime!</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E210-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1532/HSF98.20101130</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An aneurysm of the sinus of Valsalva ruptures in about 35% of all cases and only leads to acute symptoms in 25% of all patients. This paper illustrates a case of a patient who was scheduled for an elective operation due to an aneurysm of the right coronary sinus of Valsalva, which ruptured and led to the necessity of an emergency surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
